DXVK: four features upstream requires become optional (Vulkan on Metal)

Madeira, 2026-10-13, for DXVK v3.1.1 (b1a1c99ab5); zlib licence like DXVK.

KosmicKrisp (Mesa 26.2.4) has no geometryShader, no fillModeNonSolid and no
VK_EXT_depth_clip_enable; MoltenVK 1.4.2 has no geometry shaders, no
VK_EXT_depth_clip_enable and no cull distances. Upstream refuses such a device
("Device does not support required feature ..."), so the DXGI factory lists
no adapter. With this patch the device is created, one warning per missing
feature is logged, and:
- geometryShader: D3D11 geometry shaders are not bound (BindShader drops
  them, one warning); those draws run with the vertex/domain shader output.
- fillModeNonSolid: wireframe rasterizer states draw solid.
- VK_EXT_depth_clip_enable: depth clip is expressed through depthClampEnable
  (Vulkan clips when depth clamp is off), in pipelines and pipeline libraries.
- shaderCullDistance: not enabled; a shader that writes cull distances
  fails to compile into a pipeline.
Devices that have the features take the upstream paths unchanged.

